    <selectionEntry id="fd33-9271-18e9-4233" name="Armoured Fist Marshal" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Armoured Fist Marshal" id="74b2-ef79-7824-de3b" hidden="false">
          <description>An Armoured Marshal is an upgrade for a Vehicle with the Imperial Army (Solar Auxilia) Faction and Sub-faction. No model may take more than one, but several models may each take one, within each upgrade's own limits. An upgrade uses no Force Organisation slot. A Marshal bought for a Lord of War counts towards that slot's cost for the 25% Lords of War and Primarch limit.

• The model may make the Concentrated Fire Advanced Reaction.
• It may take a Nuncio-Vox for +10 points and a Cognis-Signum for +15 points.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Concentrated Fire" id="3da1-4b1a-188f-3a02" hidden="false" targetId="fb11-9321-0bc8-4b0e" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <selectionEntryGroups>
        <selectionEntryGroup name="May take" hidden="false" id="0916-2dac-582a-8ed9">
          <entryLinks>
            <entryLink id="3866-24f4-ca98-19ad" name="Nuncio-Vox" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="005e-aae6-ddac-bb45" type="selectionEntry">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="6c6b-a09f-82ad-c499" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="10"/>
              </costs>
            </entryLink>
            <entryLink id="b942-b442-41e1-6e46" name="Cognis-Signum" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="93b3-2d66-f7a3-be42" type="selectionEntry">
              <constraints>
                <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="e8f0-ba7b-d147-ed8b" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
              </constraints>
              <costs>
                <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="15"/>
              </costs>
            </entryLink>
          </entryLinks>
        </selectionEntryGroup>
      </selectionEntryGroups>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="96e0-12c9-688a-c9b3" name="Dictatii Marshal" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="roster" shared="true" id="fbee-9ed5-5a17-eb39" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Dictatii Marshal" id="3f9c-7b01-e2b2-3c15" hidden="false">
          <description>An Armoured Marshal is an upgrade for a Vehicle with the Imperial Army (Solar Auxilia) Faction and Sub-faction. No model may take more than one, but several models may each take one, within each upgrade's own limits. An upgrade uses no Force Organisation slot. A Marshal bought for a Lord of War counts towards that slot's cost for the 25% Lords of War and Primarch limit.

• The model gains Void Shields (2), +1 BS and +2 Hull Points.
• Friendly Solar Auxilia models within 12" automatically pass Morale and Pinning tests.
• The model has a Flare Shield at no cost, and may not buy one from any other source.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Void Shields (X)" id="e764-0a79-d61d-3a80" hidden="false" targetId="c503-f5b8-3da0-16e6" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Void Shields (2)"/>
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink id="4c43-bbf1-e5e0-b16b" name="Flare Shield" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="0e77-6285-22bb-1534" type="selectionEntry">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="4583-5f61-c2f0-7c5e" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="071d-1a84-3092-08d8" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="3c41-2f95-a3e8-e491" name="Ordnance Corps Marshal" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Ordnance Corps Marshal" id="f12a-160c-e10c-6233" hidden="false">
          <description>An Armoured Marshal is an upgrade for a Vehicle with the Imperial Army (Solar Auxilia) Faction and Sub-faction. No model may take more than one, but several models may each take one, within each upgrade's own limits. An upgrade uses no Force Organisation slot. A Marshal bought for a Lord of War counts towards that slot's cost for the 25% Lords of War and Primarch limit.

• The model gains Blitz Barrage and has a Nuncio-Vox.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Blitz Barrage" id="8a95-1d75-c312-88f3" hidden="false" targetId="1003-277b-d7d6-5ea5" type="rule"/>
      </infoLinks>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink id="b03c-2100-a0c9-a672" name="Nuncio-Vox" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="005e-aae6-ddac-bb45" type="selectionEntry">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="0597-151a-3fe9-100a" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="5450-f4a0-e3c9-f923" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="38ae-c251-b8bb-a974" name="Heavy Void Armour (entire unit)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Heavy Void Armour (entire unit)" id="2ea0-b218-3202-1684" hidden="false">
          <description>Every model in the unit exchanges its Void Armour for Heavy Void Armour.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink id="0344-841c-578e-d6cf" name="Heavy Void Armour" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" targetId="523c-d7fb-5288-fe13" type="selectionEntry">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="8f28-d104-c193-1947" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="e87f-7d40-c777-728e" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="866c-8b40-319f-f576" name="Twin-Linked (one ranged weapon)" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
      <rules>
        <rule name="Twin-Linked (one ranged weapon)" id="8a97-74e2-6860-c217" hidden="false">
          <description>One of the Arvus Transport's ranged weapons gains Twin-linked.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <costs>
        <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
      </costs>
    </selectionEntry>
  </sharedSelectionEntries>
  <sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
    <selectionEntryGroup id="9da6-635b-fa1d-2c2b" name="Cohort Doctrines" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="bf99-af3b-5096-cd3c" type="max"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry id="fe04-c096-f846-a6fd" name="Reborn Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="71" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="05af-452b-0e23-3b16" name="Reborn Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="71" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• All models with the Infantry Unit Type in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine gain a bonus of +1 to their Leadership Characteristic, to a maximum of Leadership 10, and the Stubborn Special Rule.
• When making a Shooting Attack during any Game Turn in which the attacking unit has not Moved, a unit from a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may re-roll all failed To Hit rolls of ‘1’.

Limitations
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than a single Auxilia Armoured Tercio.
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than a single Auxilia Artillery Tercio.
• All models with the Infantry Unit Type in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine count their Initiative as ‘1’ for the purposes of determining the distance moved when Running, when rolling as part of a Sweeping Advance, or when making a Move as part of any Reaction; and when determining which Initiative Step they would attack in during an Assault their Initiative Characteristic is considered to be one lower than normal.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="3624-316b-4ed4-d5d1" name="Ultramar Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="70" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="e0ba-7a66-48a3-da09" name="Ultramar Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="70" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine uses the Organisation chart shown below to select all Auxilia Rifle Sections instead of the one found in the unit profile and may include up to 6 units.
• All Solar Auxilia Rifle Sections and Solar Auxilia Line Command Sections gain a bonus of +1 to all To Hit rolls made during Shooting Attacks when all models in the unit are in base contact with at least one other model from the same unit.

Ultramar Pattern Auxilia Rifle Tercio Organisation Chart
An Ultramar Pattern Auxilia Infantry Tercio must include the following units:
• 0-1 Line Command Section
• 1-6 Auxilia Rifle Sections

Limitations
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not select Dedicated Transports for any Solar Auxilia Rifle Sections or Solar Auxilia Line Command Sections.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="1974-9f9a-5b14-e449" name="Armoured Fist Pattern Cohorts (Check Limitations manually)" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="71" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="a28b-aeef-6d88-8985" name="Armoured Fist Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="71" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select Auxilia Armoured Tercios as Troops choices. An Auxilia Armoured Tercio selected as a Troops choice may only consist of a single unit. Auxilia Armoured Tercios selected as Compulsory Troop Choices in a Primary Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine gain the Line Unit Sub-type.
• In a Primary Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine, a single Solar Auxilia Armoured Command Section composed of only a single Leman Russ Command Tank, must be selected as a HQ choice. This Leman Russ Command Tank gains the Cohort Doctrines special rule and must be selected as the army’s Warlord and must use the Armoured Legate Warlord trait (see below). A model with the Vehicle Unit Type must be selected as the Warlord of an army using this Cohort Doctrine, regardless of any rules which would require a model to be selected as the army’s Warlord (note this means that some units and Characters cannot be selected as part of this army):
• The first time in a game that any models with the Infantry Unit Type Disembark from their own Dedicated Transport, they gain the Relentless Special Rule until the end of that turn.

Warlord Trait: Armoured Legate
A Warlord with this Warlord Trait gains the Cohort Doctrines special rule, a 5+ Invulnerable Save and increases its BS by +1.

Limitations
• All units composed entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type must begin the battle Embarked on a model with the Transport Unit Sub-type or in Reserves, unless the unit has the Mechanised Unit Sub-type. (THIS MUST BE MANUALLY CHECKED)
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include any models with a Movement Characteristic of 0 or '-'.
• An army which includes at least one Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not select any Fortification choices.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="bfd2-7016-f5fe-be6a" name="Penal Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="72" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="dc68-cb01-b862-110a" name="Penal Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="72" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• All models in a unit from a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine that include models with the Tercio special rule also gain the Furious Charge (1) special rule.
• Any model in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may replace a lasrifle or volkite charger with a lascarbine, lasgun, stubcarbine, autorifle or shotgun for no additional points cost. In addition, one Auxilia in any Solar Auxilia Rifle Section may replace a lasrifle with a heavy stubber for +5 points per model.
• All models selected as part of a Solar Auxilia Rifle Section gain the Feel No Pain (6+) special rule – this does not stack with any other variant of this special rule and if the unit has access to any other Feel No Pain (X) special rule, the controlling player must select one to use.

• Any model in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may replace a Close Combat Weapon with a Chainsword for +1 point per model.
Limitations
• All models in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine with the Close-order Unit Sub-type lose that Unit Sub-type.
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than one Auxilia Veletaris Tercio.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="021e-6841-7375-7862" name="Feral Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="72" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="1a4f-9ea3-092f-f00e" name="Feral Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="72" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• Any unit made up entirely of models with the Infantry Unit Type may be given the Fear (1) special rule for a cost of +25 points per unit.
• All units that include one or more models with the Tercio special rule gain the Counter-attack (1) special rule while ‘In Formation’.

• All models with the Infantry Unit Type from a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine gain a bonus of +1 to their Weapon Skill, to a maximum of 5, for the duration of any player turn in which they make a Successful Charge.
• Any model in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may replace a Bayonet with a Chain Bayonet for +1 point per model.
• Any model with the Character Unit Sub-type in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may exchange a Close Combat Weapon for a Chain Axe for +2 points per model.
Limitations
• All units in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine that begin the controlling player’s Assault phase with an enemy unit that is a valid target for a Charge must declare a Charge. If more than one enemy unit is a valid target, the controlling player chooses which enemy unit is the target of the Charge.
• All other Detachments in an army with the Loyalist Allegiance that includes a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine will consider the Detachment with this Cohort Doctrine to be Distrusted Allies, regardless of the normal result of the Allies Matrix.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="d9a0-4875-fb75-f9a9" name="Siege Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="73" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="bf71-d394-4968-20e3" name="Siege Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="73" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select Auxilia Artillery Tercios and Solar Auxilia Armoured Batteries as both Elites and Heavy Support choices. In addition, they may select Solar Auxilia Artillery Battery squads as both Heavy Support and Fortification choices.
• When a model from a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine makes a Shooting Attack with any weapon with the Barrage and/or Blast special rules, the controlling player may choose to re-roll the Scatter dice (but not any D6 rolled to determine the distance of any scatter).

• Any unit eligible to purchase a Dedicated Transport may instead elect to purchase a Defence Line without occupying a Fortification Force Organisation slot, but the cost in points must be counted towards the army total as usual. A unit which has selected a Defence Line in this way counts as having purchased a Dedicated Transport.
Limitations
• All units in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine with the option to select a Dedicated Transport must select that option at the normal cost in points – but do not have to start the battle Embarked on that Dedicated Transport.
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may only be selected for an army's Primary Detachment.

Liber Imperatus addition
• Units that may take an Aurox Transport may take a Solar Auxilia Termite Assault Drill instead, and units that may take a Dracosan Armoured Transport may take an Auxilia Hades Breaching Drill instead.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="e0e8-1223-7794-2e95" name="Iron Pattern Cohort" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="73" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="4d43-43ca-68bb-2608" name="Iron Pattern Cohort" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="73" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select Castellax Maniples* and Thallax Squads* as Elites choices.
• A Legate Marshal, Auxilia Marshal or Auxilia Captain in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select a cortex controller* for +15 points each.
• A Legate Marshal in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine gains the Master of Automata special rule.
*Unit profiles and rules for these can be found in Liber Mechanicum.
• An army that uses the Cohort Doctrine: Iron Pattern Cohort may take a single unit with the Corrupted Engine Unit Sub-type. An army can only include a maximum of one unit with the Corrupted Engine Unit Sub-type chosen in this manner.

Limitations
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than a single Auxilia Armoured Tercio.
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than a single Auxilia Artillery Tercio.

Liber Imperatus addition
• Enginseer Auxilia Sections gain the Line Sub-type and may take a Triaros Armoured Conveyor as a Dedicated Transport (Liber Mechanicum rules and cost).</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="a09b-28bd-8ffc-f4f0" name="Solar Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="70" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule id="dd51-13b7-cd51-37ef" name="Solar Pattern Cohorts" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="70" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select Auxilia Veletaris Tercios as Troops choices.
• All units selected as part of an Auxilia Veletaris Tercio in a Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select an Arvus Transport as a Dedicated Transport.
• All units in an Auxilia Veletaris Tercio selected as a Troops choice gain the Line Unit Sub-type.

Limitations
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than a single Auxilia Armoured Tercio.
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than a single Auxilia Artillery Tercio.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Reconnaissance Pattern Cohorts" hidden="false" id="7e09-aae1-d5ff-d43e" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="179">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Reconnaissance Pattern Cohorts" id="7e04-8329-9f52-1bc1" hidden="false" publicationId="d882-d2a-5da1-92c4" page="179">
              <description>Effects
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may select Solar Auxilia Hermes Light Sentinel Squadrons as Troops choices. Solar Auxilia Hermes Light Sentinel Squadrons selected as Compulsory Troops choices gain the Line Unit Sub-type.
• Solar Auxilia Hermes Veletaris Squadrons in this Detachment gain the Outflank special rule.
• Aethon Heavy Sentinel Squadrons may include up to 4 additional Aethon Heavy Sentinels instead of up to 2 additional Aethon Heavy Sentinels.

Limitations
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than a single Auxilia Armoured Tercio.
• A Detachment using this Cohort Doctrine may not include more than a single Auxilia Artillery Tercio.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="f345-3c34-653e-07df" name="Apostle Pattern Cohorts" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="equalTo" value="0" field="selections" scope="force" childId="f9c0-0c5a-3e24-58c7" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Apostle Pattern Cohorts" id="af1a-35c4-074a-f9b5" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• Possessed Auxilia may be taken as Troops.
• Mutated Spawn may be taken as Fast Attack choices (see the Imperialis Militia conversion).
• Auxilia Battle Psykers may take the Anathemata Psychic Discipline instead of a Core Psychic Discipline.
• Any unit made up entirely of Infantry, Cavalry, Dreadnought or Mechanised models may gain the Corrupted Sub-type for +25 points per unit, losing Close-Order if it had it. Attached models such as Medicae are upgraded separately.
• Any Character may exchange a Power Weapon for a Tainted Axe, Tainted Blade or Tainted Maul for +5 points each.

Limitations
• The Detachment must have the Traitor Allegiance.
• It may include no more than one Auxilia Armoured Tercio and no more than one Auxilia Artillery Tercio.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="80f0-7f67-aaac-cafb" name="Echoes of Lost Glory" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Echoes of Lost Glory" id="58e4-d717-6a6a-3c0c" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• All units in the Detachment gain Advanced Weapons.
• Any Infantry unit without the Monstrous Sub-type may replace its Void Armour or Reinforced Void Armour with Heavy Void Armour for +30 points per unit.
• Any model may exchange a Blast Pistol for a Needle Pistol (free), or a Heavy Bolter for a Needle Cannon (+5 points each) or a Volkite Culverin (+10 points each).
• Any Infantry model may exchange a Volkite Charger for an Assault Needler (+2 points each), and any model may exchange a Rotor Cannon for a Needle Cannon (+10 points each). If taken, every model in the unit must make the same exchange.

Limitations
• The army's Warlord must have the Cohort Doctrines Special Rule.
• Every Tercio in the Detachment that can include a Command Section of any kind must do so.
• If the Warlord is removed as a casualty, every unit in the Detachment not locked in combat must take a Morale check. Units that cannot take or automatically pass Morale checks (Vehicles, Fearless and so on) ignore this.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="6f6d-46a9-3fe2-531e" name="Legion-Sworn Cohorts" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="notInstanceOf" value="0" field="selections" scope="ancestor" childId="d4f2-6da5-b6de-06ec" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Legion-Sworn Cohorts" id="dd52-8e24-c1ec-6f11" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• The Detachment counts as one Level of Alliance higher with one chosen Space Marine Legion Faction.
• Any model may exchange a Lasrifle for a Bolter for free, or a Laspistol for a Bolt Pistol for +2 points each.

Limitations
• Only an Allied Detachment may take this Cohort Doctrine.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="51af-a678-4899-1c2e" name="Linebreaker Pattern Cohorts" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Linebreaker Pattern Cohorts" id="2bfc-f7f2-3045-ea40" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• Solar Auxilia Furibundus Dreadnought Talons and Solar Auxilia Extremis Boarding Rig Sections may be taken as Troops.
• Those taken as Compulsory Troops gain the Line Sub-type.

Limitations
• The Detachment may not include Auxilia Armoured Tercios, Solar Auxilia Macharius Heavy Tank Squadrons, Macharius Omega Heavy Tanks or Praetorian Heavy Tank Squadrons.
• The Detachment may not take Fortifications.
• An army whose Primary Detachment uses this Doctrine may not roll to Seize the Initiative.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="6ad7-990b-d949-0f57" name="Pioneer Companies" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Pioneer Companies" id="65bd-bcd4-fc9e-7011" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• Solar Auxilia Pioneer Sections gain the Line Sub-type and Infiltrate.
• Auxilia Infantry Support Tercios made up only of Solar Auxilia Ancillary Command Sections and/or Pioneer Sections may be taken as Compulsory Troops.
• All units in an Auxilia Veletaris Tercio gain Scout.
• Aethon Heavy Sentinel Squadrons may be taken as non-Compulsory Troops.
• If the Primary Detachment uses this Doctrine, the player may re-roll the roll for first turn and the roll to Seize the Initiative.

Limitations
• The Detachment may not take Fortifications, except those bought in place of Dedicated Transports for Pioneer Sections.
• The Detachment may include no more than one Auxilia Armoured Tercio.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="c3ab-387a-c134-9d22" name="Scourge Pattern Cohorts" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="true">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="instanceOf" value="0" field="selections" scope="ancestor" childId="d4f2-6da5-b6de-06ec" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Scourge Pattern Cohorts" id="2bf6-b6d7-6bc0-bc4f" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• Solar Auxilia Hellhound Flame Tank Squadrons may be taken as non-Compulsory Troops.
• Any model may exchange a Flamer or Heavy Flamer for a Toxiferran Flamer for free.
• Any Character may take Rad Grenades for +10 points.
• Any Auxilia Rapier Carrier with Quad Launchers may take Phosphex Canister Shot for +20 points each.
• Any Auxilia Malcador Infernus may replace its Centreline Mounted Inferno Cannon with a Centreline Mounted Chem Destroyer for +25 points each.

Limitations
• Only a Primary Detachment may take this Doctrine, and the army may not include an Allied Detachment.
• The Detachment may not take Fortifications.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="8141-eb9e-4bc3-5fb8" name="Steel Fury Pattern Cohorts" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Steel Fury Pattern Cohorts" id="5c2f-2e89-8cc7-0006" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• The Detachment must take a Lord of War in place of a Primarch on the Crusade Force Organisation Chart. It gains Cohort Doctrines, must be the army's Warlord regardless of any other rule, and must take the Super-Heavy Armoured Legate Warlord Trait.
• Solar Auxilia Macharius Heavy Tank Squadrons may be taken as Elites.

Limitations
• Every Lords of War Detachment in the army must have the Solar Auxilia Sub-faction.
• The Detachment must contain more Vehicle units than non-Vehicle units.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry id="4d2c-cd73-6985-50f0" name="Valkyria Pattern Cohorts" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <rules>
            <rule name="Valkyria Pattern Cohorts" id="7c2a-5080-ba6c-ffe0" hidden="false">
              <description>Effects
• Solar Auxilia Aello Gunship Squadrons may be taken as Heavy Support.
• Units that may take an Aurox Transport may take an Arvus Transport instead.
• Units that may take a Chimera Transport may take an Auxilia Aello or Auxilia Kelaino instead.
• Flyer Transport Vehicles from this Detachment in Reserves may automatically arrive at the start of their first turn without a Reserves roll. If they do not, they roll for Reserves normally from turn two.

Limitations
• Every unit made up entirely of Infantry must start the battle Embarked on a Transport or in Reserves.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup name="Penal Weapons" id="e046-e15f-16a9-0cf3" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" defaultSelectionEntryId="6d17-07d2-d48a-0c7f" flatten="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="2b66-3cdf-0580-01ad" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Autorifle" hidden="false" id="d41f-94f2-71e8-2c8d" collective="false" targetId="57dd-dff6-d173-3bf1" type="selectionEntry"/>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Lascarbine" hidden="false" id="7268-fe96-38e8-2dfa" collective="false" targetId="d68e-ce5a-000c-c322" type="selectionEntry"/>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Lasgun" hidden="false" id="303b-635b-d2b9-ebea" collective="false" targetId="376e-c5d6-99c3-49c9" type="selectionEntry"/>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Shotgun" hidden="false" id="2c80-6674-b45e-cda5" collective="false" targetId="f0aa-947f-f493-f566" type="selectionEntry"/>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Stubcarbine" hidden="false" id="31f0-db94-dc6e-52d5" collective="false" targetId="a7cc-88cb-c6e8-6d4c" type="selectionEntry"/>
      </entryLinks>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" value="true" field="hidden">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="lessThan" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="bfd2-7016-f5fe-be6a" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
    <selectionEntryGroup id="fe57-5aeb-f6a6-f137" name="Warlord Traits (Solar Auxilia)" hidden="true" collective="false" import="true">
      <modifiers>
        <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="greaterThan" value="0" field="selections" scope="parent" childId="0176-56a3-d590-b103" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
        <modifier type="set" field="dd62-6a5d-cc74-cd59" value="0">
          <conditions>
            <condition type="greaterThan" value="0" field="selections" scope="parent" childId="1ebb-8e01-7d58-9d99" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
          </conditions>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <constraints>
        <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="dd62-6a5d-cc74-cd59" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
      </constraints>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Bitter Blood" hidden="false" id="6cbf-0c9c-3087-1aee">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="deb8-376c-6a34-c1bd" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Bitter Blood" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="665e-4284-429a-2fbb">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord gains +1 WS, Fleet (1) and Hatred (Everything!). An Independent Character Warlord may buy one Solar Auxilia Companion Section or Tactical Command Section as a Household Retinue, which loses Tercio. While the Warlord is with it, its models gain +1 WS, Fleet (1), Hatred (Everything!) and the Line Sub-type. The Warlord must deploy with it and may not voluntarily leave. While the Warlord lives, the army gains one extra Reaction in the opponent's Assault phase.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Co-ordinated Devastation" hidden="false" id="07d3-eb2f-e4f2-6ccc">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="8b17-98b2-b226-da17" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Co-ordinated Devastation" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="272e-01a1-2286-649a">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord's ranged weapons gain +6" Range. At the start of its Shooting phase, the Warlord may nominate an enemy unit within 30" and line of sight; the Warlord, a Tercio unit it has joined and any units In Formation with that unit gain +1 To Hit against it that phase. While the Warlord lives, the army gains one extra Reaction in the opponent's Shooting phase.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Super-Heavy Armoured Legate" hidden="true" id="15fe-1f25-243f-f97c">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="hidden" value="false">
              <conditions>
                <condition type="equalTo" value="1" field="selections" scope="force" childId="8141-eb9e-4bc3-5fb8" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" percentValue="false"/>
              </conditions>
            </modifier>
          </modifiers>
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="7f55-b9ce-e111-0148" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Super-Heavy Armoured Legate" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="aa17-8641-5642-ecab">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord gains the Dictatii Marshal upgrade at no cost, and +1 BS on top of any other bonus.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Void Master" hidden="false" id="72ef-ce9a-9091-b0aa">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="4f69-5f9b-95b1-f9a0" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Void Master" typeId="a0e6-a7b4-d55d-85b8" typeName="Warlord Trait" hidden="false" id="079c-d0c5-401f-65c8">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="c68e-2cda-b67b-baca">The Warlord gains Move Through Cover and Stubborn, ignores Debris Terrain's movement penalty, and may re-roll failed Dangerous Terrain and Hazardous Debris tests. If it is an Independent Character in a Tercio unit, these apply to that unit and every unit In Formation with it. While the Warlord lives, the army gains one extra Reaction in the opponent's Movement phase.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="Pts" typeId="d2ee-04cb-5f8a-2642" value="0"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="bf74-20ed-ddc9-8ea1" name="Solar Auxilia Command Tank" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="136" hidden="false">
      <description>A model with this Special Rule is selected as a separate unit, but during deployment must be assigned to another unit and may not be deployed as a separate unit. If multiple appropriate units are available, the Controlling Player chooses which unit a model with this Special Rule is assigned to. Once assigned to a unit, a model with this Special Rule counts as a part of that unit and may not leave the unit during play for any reason.
A model with this Special Rule must be assigned to another unit made up entirely of models with the Vehicle Unit Type purchased as part of the same Tercio.
In addition, a model with this Special Rule may still make Shooting Attacks as normal in a turn in which they use their Cognis-Signum to provide +1 Ballistic Skill to all other models in their unit, even though this would normally be prevented by using this Wargear.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="25f0-12ed-08dd-0781" name="Auxilia Artillerists" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="130" hidden="false">
      <description>A Solar Auxilia Rapier Battery must have one Auxilia Gunner per Rapier Carrier in order for all Rapier Carriers to make Shooting Attacks in the Shooting phase. If, at the start of any of the controlling player’s Shooting phases, the Solar Auxilia Rapier Battery contains fewer Auxilia Gunners than Rapier Carriers, then only a number of Rapier Carriers equal to the number of  Auxilia Gunners may make Shooting Attacks in that Shooting phase. In addition, as long as there are at least as many Auxilia Gunners in the unit as there are Rapier Carriers, then the unit cannot be Pinned, automatically passing any Pinning tests it is called upon to take without any dice being rolled (this benefit is lost immediately once the number of Auxilia Gunners is reduced to less than the number of Rapier Carriers in the unit).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a217-f49a-7a73-981d" name="Demolition Vehicle" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="131" hidden="false">
      <description>At Initiative step 10, instead of rolling To Hit as normal, a model with this Special Rule instead inflicts one automatic Hit using the profile below on any one  enemy model it is in base contact with (chosen by the player that controls the model with this special rule). Once this Hit is resolved, the model with this special rule is automatically  removed as a casualty (the removal of this model does not add any Wounds to the total used to determine which side has won the Assault).

Weapon 		Range	Str	AP	Type
Demo charge		- 	10	1	Melee, Armourbane (Melee), Instant Death, Brutal (2)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2d37-470b-462f-9c99" name="Independent Operators" publicationId="15a4-fc68-502d-48a9" page="133" hidden="false">
      <description>When deployed onto the battlefield (either at the start of the battle, when arriving from Reserves or Disembarking from a model with the Transport Sub-type), all models with this special rule in the same unit must be placed within unit coherency following the normal rules for deploying/Disembarking units, but after deployment or Disembarkation all models in the unit with this special rule are considered to have left the unit, and now form separate units of a single model each. For the remainder of the battle, a model with this special rule is considered a separate unit for all purposes and may not join other units or reform into their original unit. However, the whole unit must be removed as casualties before the opposing player scores any Victory points for the destruction of any model that was part of the unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="ae18-3eb1-72ce-7921" hidden="false">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
